# PromptForge runs with zero environment variables out of the box: with
# nothing set below, it stays in the Phase 1–6 demo mode — "signing in"
# opens a local demo account (src/lib/demo-auth.ts), data lives in
# localStorage, and the AI assist panel uses a local simulation.
#
# Set the Supabase variables to switch on real accounts + persistence.
# Set GROQ_API_KEY to switch on real AI assist calls. Each is
# independent — you can turn on one without the other.

# --- Supabase (real auth + persistence) -------------------------------------
# Create a project at https://supabase.com, run supabase/schema.sql in its
# SQL editor, then copy these from Project Settings -> API.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
#
# "Continue with Google" (login/signup pages) needs the Google provider
# turned on in Supabase: Authentication -> Providers -> Google, with a
# Google Cloud OAuth client ID/secret. Add
# https://your-project.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback as an authorized
# redirect URI on the Google Cloud OAuth client. No separate env var is
# needed here — it's config on the Supabase project, not this app.

# Only needed for admin/server-side scripts that must bypass row-level
# security (e.g. a one-off data migration). The app itself never uses this
# — never expose it to the browser (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, on purpose).
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# --- AI provider (real Improve/Rewrite/Expand/Shorten) ----------------------
# Server-only — used by src/app/api/ai/route.ts, never sent to the browser.
# Get free keys at https://console.groq.com. Uses llama-3.1-8b-instant.
#
# Set just one key to get started:
# GROQ_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key
#
# For automatic fallback across multiple keys (e.g. so a per-key daily rate
# limit doesn't take AI assist down), set up to 5 numbered keys instead.
# If a key hits its limit (HTTP 429) or is rejected, the request instantly
# retries with the next one — no code changes needed, just add more keys:
# GROQ_API_KEY_1=your-first-groq-api-key
# GROQ_API_KEY_2=your-second-groq-api-key
# GROQ_API_KEY_3=your-third-groq-api-key
# GROQ_API_KEY_4=your-fourth-groq-api-key
# GROQ_API_KEY_5=your-fifth-groq-api-key

# --- Forge AI (the floating chat panel) --------------------------------------
# Server-only — used by src/app/api/forge-ai/route.ts, never sent to the
# browser. Deliberately a SEPARATE key pool from GROQ_API_KEY_* above, so
# Forge AI's chat traffic is independent of Improve/Rewrite/Expand/Shorten/
# Critique — configure one without affecting the other. Same shape: one key,
# or up to 5 for automatic fallback.
# FORGE_AI_GROQ_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key
#
# FORGE_AI_GROQ_API_KEY_1=your-first-groq-api-key
# FORGE_AI_GROQ_API_KEY_2=your-second-groq-api-key
# FORGE_AI_GROQ_API_KEY_3=your-third-groq-api-key
# FORGE_AI_GROQ_API_KEY_4=your-fourth-groq-api-key
# FORGE_AI_GROQ_API_KEY_5=your-fifth-groq-api-key

# --- Misc --------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
